  "description": "Summary of Proposed Works\n\nThe proposed works comprise the internal reconfiguration of flat 43 within Defoe House, including the removal and reconstruction of non-structural partitions, the combination of the existing bathroom and WC into a single enlarged space, and the formation of revised room layouts.\n\nNew lightweight stud walls will be introduced to reconfigure the plan, including the extension of the bathroom into part of the existing bedroom. This allows for improved accessibility and the installation of a level-access walk-in shower. A new wardrobe alcove will be formed within the bedroom in conjunction with the revised wall layout.\n\nExisting internal doors will be removed and replaced with new full-height openings, including a wide sliding pocket door to the combined bathroom/WC and a new full-height door to the bedroom. Door widths and circulation spaces will be increased throughout to improve accessibility.\n\nAll new joinery will be designed to reflect the simple, flush-painted character of the original Barbican interiors, with existing architrave proportions and characteristic shadow gap detailing matched. Where new wall sections are formed, the characteristic Barbican flush skirting detail will be reinstated on a like-for-like basis where visible.\n\nThe bathroom will be refitted with new sanitary-ware and finishes, and the kitchen will be replaced within its existing footprint using a bespoke design informed by the character of the original Barbican kitchens, with adjustments to layout and working heights to improve usability.\n\nAll works are internal, non-structural, and will be carried out in a manner that respects the character and detailing of the original Barbican interiors.",
